{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>ויכתום [and they struck them].</b> Rabbi Moses the Kohen the Sefardi, of blessed memory, said that it should have been ויכיתום [with a yod before the third-person suffix], and likewise וידביקו גם המה [Numbers 21:23, without a yod]. But the correct view in my eyes is that it is of the doubled [hif'il] forms, and it is a strange word." "<b>עד החרמה [until Hormah].</b> A place name. And some say: until they destroyed them [reading the word as a verbal form rather than a proper noun]."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:46.413418368Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}